At Texco, we take great pride in our contribution to Australia's industrial property landscape. We believe in rewarding hard work, nurturing relationships, and fostering innovative thinking within a collaborative workplace and project environment.
We are proud to have attracted some of the best talent in the industry and are continuously seeking individuals who share our passion for industrial and commercial construction, thrive on challenges, and are motivated to learn and grow within a high-performing team.
As our project portfolio continues to expand, an exciting opportunity has become available for a proactive and detail-focused Revit Technician/Documenter to join our growing design team.
With a solid foundation in Revit and architectural documentation, you will have the opportunity to further develop your technical capabilities across a diverse range of industrial projects, whilst continuing to building your career within a collaborative and experienced team.
The opportunity on offer
As a Revit Technician/Docuemnter at Texco, you will play a critical role in supporting the delivery of industry-leading industrial developments through the production and coordination of high-quality Revit models and construction documentation.
Working closely with our Architectural Design Lead, BIM Project Leads and broader Architecture team, you will be responsible for managing project documentation from concept through to completion. Your expertise in Revit, BIM processes and technical documentation will help ensure our projects are delivered efficiently, accurately, and to the highest professional standards.
This is a hands-on technical role that offers exposure to a diverse portfolio of industrial developments, while also providing opportunities to contribute to the ongoing enhancement of Texco's Revit systems, libraries, templates and documentation standards.
Your key responsibilities will include:
- Develop, coordinate and maintain high-quality Revit models and documentation across all stages of project delivery;
- Produce accurate construction documentation, schedules and as-built drawings;
- Coordinate and integrate BIM information across multiple consultant disciplines;
- Undertake quality assurance reviews to ensure consistency, accuracy and compliance with project and company standards;
- Collaborate closely with internal stakeholders to meet project milestones and delivery deadlines;
- Support the management and maintenance of Texco's Revit technical systems and documentation standards;
- Assist with the development and enhancement of Revit families, templates, material libraries and workflows;
- Coordinate BIM submissions, construction models and project schedules;
- Liaise with consultants, contractors and project teams to resolve documentation and design issues;
- Support continuous improvement initiatives that drive efficiency, innovation and best practice across the Design team.
A bit about you
- Technical qualifications in Architecture, Building Design, Drafting or a related discipline;
- Demonstrated experience in a Revit Technician, BIM Technician or similar role within the industrial, commercial or architectural sector;
- Intermediate proficiency in Revit, with strong experience producing detailed construction and planning documentation;
- Strong understanding of BIM processes, methodologies and industry best practice;
- Sound knowledge of the National Construction Code (NCC), Australian Standards and construction detailing principles;
- Excellent attention to detail and commitment to producing high-quality documentation;
- Strong problem-solving and analytical skills;
- Ability to effectively manage competing priorities and multiple projects simultaneously;
- Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills;
- A proactive, team-oriented approach with a genuine passion for continuous improvement and technical excellence.
What makes working for us unique
We pride ourselves on our vibrant, inclusive team culture. Our team is composed of talented, like-minded self-starters who are intellectually curious and passionate about their work. Here are some of the benefits we offer in addition to a great team and working environment:
- We recognise loyalty, performance, values alignment, and outstanding achievements.
- Our stunning bespoke office in Hawthorn East offers ample off-site all-day parking nearby.
- Say goodbye to costly monthly gym memberships with access to our impressive onsite gym.
- Our leadership team is dedicated to nurturing your capabilities and passions.
- We have several internal fitness clubs catering to a range of sporting interests and athletic abilities.
- Enjoy flexible work-life balance with our Work From Home program and additional leave benefits.
- Participate in a variety of fun social activities, including Friday-night drinks, celebratory BBQs, mid and end-of-year events, wine and cheese nights, trivia nights, and more.
- Benefit from our health and wellbeing initiatives designed to support your personal and professional performance.
Join us
If you're ready to take the next step in your career and want to be part of a team that values innovation, excellence, and a supportive culture, we would love to hear from you. Apply now via our careers page to join Texco and help us continue to lead with quality and innovation
